---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="About Us — Class Schedule Maker & Gap Optimizer"
  description="Learn about our mission to eliminate dead time on college campuses, our client-side privacy architecture, and academic engineering background."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 space-y-12">
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-lg text-xs font-medium bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80 shadow-xs">
        <span>Our Mission</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-950 dark:text-white">
        Architecting Clean, Continuous Academic Schedules
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
        We built Class Schedule Maker & Gap Optimizer because university registration portals haven't evolved since 2004, leaving millions of students stranded in cognitive limbo between classes.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-950 dark:text-white">The Student Productivity Dilemma</h2>
      <p>
        Every semester, collegiate students spend hours juggling course reference numbers (CRNs), comparing disjointed PDF catalogs, and guessing section permutations on paper. The inevitable result is schedule fragmentation: arbitrary 75-minute and 2-hour gaps scattered across the week.
      </p>
      <p>
        These dead gaps are rarely long enough to settle into a focused 4-hour study session or return home, yet too long to remain actively engaged. They breed distraction, drain mental energy, and decrease academic performance. Our tool was engineered to solve this combinatorial challenge mathematically.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-[#121215] border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80 space-y-3">
      <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950 dark:text-white">Our 100% Client-Side Privacy Pledge</h3>
      <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
        Unlike corporate ed-tech services that monetize student schedules, require mandatory signups, or sell behavioral data to third-party advertisers, <strong>Class Schedule Optimizer operates 100% locally in your web browser</strong>.
      </p>
      <ul class="text-xs space-y-2 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 list-disc pl-5">
        <li>Zero user account creation or tracking cookies.</li>
        <li>Your timetable data never leaves your device and is stored strictly in your browser's private localStorage.</li>
        <li>Open access for university students worldwide at zero cost.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-950 dark:text-white">The Engineering Team</h2>
      <p>
        We are an independent collective of software architects, former collegiate teaching assistants, and STEM graduates passionate about educational ergonomics and minimalist digital tools.
      </p>
      <p>
        Questions, suggestions, or university partnership inquiries? Contact our engineering team at <a href="mailto:hello@classscheduleoptimizer.com" class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-white underline font-medium">hello@classscheduleoptimizer.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

